  "instruction": "The year policy is not_applicable_all_history: use all history. Allocate every submission to one of three balanced consecutive processing batches per queue using NTILE(3), never value RANK, equal-time shared rank, or running amount totals. Order within a queue by submitted_at ascending NULLS LAST then submission_id ascending, including NULL peers. If N=3q+r, the first r batches have q+1 rows and the rest q rows; when N<3 use batches 1..N. Return submission_id INTEGER and batch_number BIGINT ordered submission_id ascending. Queues are exact VARCHAR labels, no normalization; empty queues are absent. No episodes/status/year exclusion. submission_id must be unique globally; otherwise equal payloads with different IDs are distinct submissions. submitted_at is the only nullable input, naive timezone-free microsecond-resolution TIMESTAMP. No other domain/foreign-key restriction. All years and unknown-time submissions participate. Empty input gives no output. Batch number is a dimensionless integer.",
